## Pickman fix report — MR !1207 (branch `cherry-e50ee1acd4a`, attempt 1)

### Root cause
The failing CI jobs (`make check`, `make qcheck`) crashed with **SIGSEGV** in
`test_spl[ut_spl_test_spl_test_load_fit_full]`. The new "full" FIT loader test
(`spl_test_load_fit_full`) exercises `spl_load_fit_image()`, whose config-
selection path reaches `select_from_config()` in `boot/image-fit.c`. With
`CONFIG_FIT_BEST_MATCH=y` it calls `fit_conf_find_compat(fit, gd_fdt_blob())`,
which does `fdt_getprop(fdt, 0, ...)`. In the SPL context `gd_fdt_blob()` is
**NULL** (no control DTB), so libfdt dereferences a NULL pointer and the
process dies with signal 11. The "simple" FIT loader never hit this, which is
why the crash only surfaced once the "full"-loader test was added.

### Responsible commit
`test: spl: add unit test for the "full" FIT loader` (cherry-picked
`e41a770f3800`). It is the commit that first drives the full loader through
this path, so the fix belongs here to keep the series bisect-safe.

### Change made
A one-line guard in `select_from_config()` (`boot/image-fit.c`), so the
best-match lookup only runs when a control FDT actually exists, otherwise it
falls back to the default configuration:

```c
if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_FIT_BEST_MATCH) && !fit_uname_config &&
    gd_fdt_blob())
        ret = fit_conf_find_compat(fit, gd_fdt_blob());
```

The change was folded into that commit (now `f199dfba856`) with a `[pickman]`
note appended to its message. `boot/image-fit.c | 3 ++-`.

